1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,504
May every website of an approved merchant take payments?

2
00:00:03,554 --> 00:00:08,232
A market licenses the company, but every stall is still inspected on its own.

3
00:00:08,282 --> 00:00:14,064
Each of a merchant's websites is a sales point, and it starts as a draft that cannot take money.

4
00:00:14,114 --> 00:00:20,472
Its return addresses must be secure and on its own site, so a payment can never send the buyer somewhere else.

5
00:00:20,522 --> 00:00:23,832
A bank admin checks the site and records the result.

6
00:00:23,882 --> 00:00:28,776
The deal says which cards the website takes, and how much it may take per payment and per day.

7
00:00:28,826 --> 00:00:34,152
Only with an active merchant, a passed check and at least one card can the website be switched on.

8
00:00:34,202 --> 00:00:41,040
And before taking any money, every part of the system asks one question: may this website take a payment right now?

9
00:00:41,090 --> 00:00:43,992
Next: how the bank's fee is decided.
